After an hour of shoddy debugging and slogging I confirmed that a conditional
was missing, as when it is included, the macro NWDEFAULTDIR is printed with
debugging fprintf statements and such, I can proceed and I know that [[no]] is
definitely seeing the [[noweb.cfg]] file that was the original complaint when I
tried to compile the PDF.

Why would I want to [[load_nwfile("tangle")]] or [[load_nwfile("weave")]] when I
call [[no]]? I assume that either the operation is meant to select the
subcommand, or something else is wrong with the implementation of [[no]] at the
moment.

Anyways, apparently [[2]] is the correct error code and something else is going
on with the system that is preventing it from loading noweb files properly,
especially [[weave]] or [[tangle]]! I need to compile the project with dubugging
symbols and see what is happening when [[load_nwfile]] is called.

GDB isn't helping me because the debugging symbols and whatnot I compiled
aren't nicely linked to my source files. I think that's because of the way I'm
using GNU Make. That will also require debugging before a final release!

The reason this fails is because the preprocessor macro [[nw_unix]] was undefined,
causing the macro [[Sys_dirsep]] be defined as [[\\]], causing the file lookup
to always fail when looking for [[noweb.cfg]]. Recompiling with [[nw_unix]]
defined should allow everything to work.
